 "how": "the six modes, the tick and the ground plane, computed by main on main's own matrices T6, S6, U (checks/physical_c8_tick_higgs.py, K1 to K4, K7): under k = 3a + 4b, T6 = diag(1, -i) (x) diag(1, w, w) and F6 = F2 (x) conj(F3), so U = A2 (x) A3 with A2 the lane's matrix; the characteristic polynomials are lambda^2 - lambda + 1 and (lambda - 1)(lambda^2 + 1), that of U is (lambda^2 - lambda + 1)(lambda^4 - lambda^2 + 1), U has order 12 and the parity's odd plane carries the phases +-pi/3; S6^2 = -i P; the tick T6 S6 K squares to U and exchanges v+ and v-; each of the lifts Z^3, X^3, Z^3 X^3 sends v+ a third onto itself, nowhere onto v-, two thirds out of the ground plane, and Z^3 X^3 = -X^3 Z^3; the bubble averaged over the four lifts is a multiple of the identity, so the mass matrix is scalar on the ground plane E and every unit vector of E is a ground direction of the quadratic problem (the twisted-circle statement is elementary); the Hermitian forms on E kept by the tick are the multiples of the identity; the tick fixes no ray of E; the pairs exchanged by it are alpha I + kappa eps J with J = (U - U^dagger)/(2i sin(pi/6)); the real polynomials invariant under the common phase, U and the tick are, at degree four, A N^2 + B Delta^2 and no others, whose minima at fixed N are the two eigenlines for B < 0, the equal-magnitude circle for B > 0, everything for B = 0",
